{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion","id":1290829,"title":"Lunar vs Solar Combat (Dexterity Charms Preview Discussion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-22T10:57:18-08:00","id":1290829,"title":"Lunar vs Solar Combat (Dexterity Charms Preview Discussion)","content":"I\u2019ve been looking at the Lunar Charm preview and I have to say it\u2019s very exciting. Thought it would be fun to have a place to model/compare solar vs lunar combat. At first glance, and as l read, I will say that in 3E the gap between the two is very small. Lunars seem to have a great deal more versatility (which makes sense) that is reflected in their charms in a big way. On the other hand they lack the giant combat effects that the Solars (And Dragonblooded even) have deep in their tree. Both Lunars and Terrestrials have more close range multi attack withering options it seems than solars and Lunars have a charm that discounts artifact cost\u2014 which I suspect is something solars probably have too but which hasn\u2019t yet been published. The charms don\u2019t feel \u2018worse\u2019 in the annoying way they did in 2e, they feel different, broader in some ways but narrower in others and as I said, their high level effects are more versatile than situationally specific and powerful. Their defensive Charms are pretty impressive to, they have subtly different (and evocative and creative) analogs of most solar defensive effects, and a few neat tricks of their own. <br /> Without having run a combat I\u2019d say I\u2019d give a lunar even odds against a solar of similar experience, not quite as potent but close enough that the element of chance could swing things either way. <br /> <br /> What were other folks\u2019 perceptions/likes/dislikes?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:10:08-08:00","id":1290837,"title":"","content":"I think we will need to see Strength or Stamina to get a real idea of where a Combat Lunar is sitting. I think the comparison to a Dawn at the same Essence level is gonna be the Full Moon with two favored Attributes and decent investment in both, but Lunars certainly have good stuff. <br /> <br /> Some of the costs and effects I am maybe a bit wary of but they're all pretty interesting. The fact Lunar thrown seems to have the ability to make Onslaught that can't be easily removed seems pretty neat, but some of their Onslaught manipulation feels very finicky. Not that Solar's aren't as well obviously.<br /> <br /> I will echo on a reread your observation that most Lunar Effects are 'bread and butter', with their only really big effects being chaining their Withering Flurry into Octopus and Spider Barrage (perfect for Lunar Dio hitting the punch rush and turning someone into powder) and their really powerful Blazing Solar Bolt equivalent.<br /> <br /> Dexterity is also really reliant on being ahead in Initiative, but also has tricks to let you do that. I think that might be where De and Stamina combine well; Dex protects you while you're ahead and then once you Decisive you can transfer to Stamina as you build up your Initiative lead again.<br /> <br /> At least from my observation<br /> <br /> I will say one thing I dislike is that they have Hail Shattering Practice and Five Fold Bulwark Stance basically straight up, with their version being cheaper in Bulwark and their Hail Shattering being cheaper at 4 or more 1s iirc, but those charms were already some of Solar's most powerful defensive abilities","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 02-22-2019, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:25:03-08:00","id":1290844,"title":"","content":"Yeah but their hail shattering practice is restricted to 1s\u2014 so much less effective and utter trash against a solar combatant. Also it\u2019s not modular, if they only need to subtract one success they pay 3m if they want to subtract 3 they pay 3m. Solars pay for what they need, and you really shouldn\u2019t ever need to buy off that many successes except in super fringe cases because both charms relay on the attacker rolling a bunch of 1s (or 1s or 2s).<br /> <br /> Their FFBS is also more restricted (having the same holes as the solar version plus not negating penalties from crippling or prone), but I agree it could stand to cost about the same\u2014 since it works for Defense not just Parry. Feels like splitting hairs at this point though. Their Parry perfect, for instance, is notably worse\u2014 while their Evasion perfect is better than their Parry perfect but less absolute than SSE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:54:11-08:00","id":1290859,"title":"","content":"To be fair, only Useless against Solar Melee. There's at least 4 other charm combat styles to choose as a Solar. It is bad against a Solar Melee but basically everything is bad against Solar Melee. <br /> <br /> I recognize this feels like I'm shifting goalpost since I'm comparing it to Solar Melee charms but that's not the intent, more the observation that not every Solar uses Melee. So yeah, limited against Solar Melee but not every Solar.<br /> <br /> Also to be fair to their FFBS, Lunars have reflexive, at any point rise from prone for 1m, 1i. At Dex 2, E1 so it's available to the same build as their FFBS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:12:08-08:00","id":1290869,"title":"","content":"I'd think Many-Armed Warrior Panoply as more Lunar than Solar.<br /> <br /> For one thing, Solars have a harder time growing additional arms. For another, Solars specialize into Abilities, especially Dawns who pick an attack Ability for their Supernal.<br /> <br /> Lunars who prefer Artifacts and Evocations may want to have more artifact weapons than Solars, and they're assisted in this by having more artifacts in rotation among the Silver Pact, which is also making more artifact weapons right now than the Solars are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:26:35-08:00","id":1290872,"title":"","content":"Counterpoint: Fate Stay Night Gilgamesh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:28:05-08:00","id":1290873,"title":"","content":"Hmmm I will probably make an entire thread about this myself once the final book is out, but I agree with flare in that we at least need to see the full range of combat options first.<br /> <br /> And social for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:35:22-08:00","id":1290875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1290869#post1290869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd think Many-Armed Warrior Panoply as more Lunar than Solar.<br /> <br /> For one thing, Solars have a harder time growing additional arms. For another, Solars specialize into Abilities, especially Dawns who pick an attack Ability for their Supernal.<br /> <br /> Lunars who prefer Artifacts and Evocations may want to have more artifact weapons than Solars, and they're assisted in this by having more artifacts in rotation among the Silver Pact, which is also making more artifact weapons right now than the Solars are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though I do agree\u2014 after a fashion, and notwithstanding the fact that you decided I needed someone to explain basic mechanics to me, I don\u2019t know that either of those things precludes solars from having effects that make attunment less of a burden. Not so much a \u201cI can cheaply attune more artifacts\u201d but a \u201cartifacts are less difficult to attune\u201d or something to reflect that sort of dynamic. I\u2019m unsure what ability I\u2019d slot that charm into, probably Integrity or Occult, but it doesn\u2019t feel right in Occult. It doesn\u2019t even really feel right in craft. Maybe a single ability charm that reduces the cost of attuning to a given weapon by a set amount something like the athletics charms that creates motes that can be spent offsetting attunement. <br /> <br /> I generally agree with your point Flare, I think the bigger gap, however, is the fact that hail shattering practice can count 1s and 2s, which means it has a 20% chance of working on a give dice, while the lunar only has a 10%. Even terrestrials have a similar effect in Brawl (blade deflecting Palm) it seems like it\u2019s something of a combat bread and butter thing. Not trying to invalidate your take or even disagree with it, just clarifying why it didn\u2019t bug me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:45:50-08:00","id":1290878,"title":"","content":"Birds-Fall-From-Flock Targeting seems to be really good. Like, REALLY good. (although admittedly, useless against one powerful foe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/242-mindworm-jim","name":"Mindworm Jim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:12:44-08:00","id":1290887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1290872#post1290872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counterpoint: Fate Stay Night Gilgamesh</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have gone for Sengoku Basara's interpretation of Date Masamune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:22:51-08:00","id":1290891,"title":"","content":"I might have misspoken. More than simple &quot;multiple&quot; artifact weapons, I was thinking of multiple <i>kinds</i> of weapons. A Melee-Supernal Solar <i>might </i>have two or more swords, if one sword just isn't enough, but a Lunar has a little more incentive to have a magical sword <i>and</i> a magical bow, since Strength and Dexterity Charms will apply equally to both, while Evocations offer a way to focus on fighting a sword or bow more than Strength and Dexterity Charms generally allow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-22-2019, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:58:23-08:00","id":1290900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mindworm Jim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1290878#post1290878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Birds-Fall-From-Flock Targeting seems to be really good. Like, REALLY good. (although admittedly, useless against one powerful foe)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but it\u2019s the kind of charm that can end a Wyld Hunt for sure, and in short order. Combine that with Octopus and Spider Barrage as well, so if all your enemies declare a ton of defensive charms, yay, they just wasted sixty motes and oh still pick the weakest one and annihilate them. They all try to conserve motes by not spending any, and therefore not waste any? Octopus and Spider Barrage every single one of them with some kind of strength based damage adder. At least I think that\u2019s possible I haven\u2019t triple checked everything yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:54:34-08:00","id":1291076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1290900#post1290900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but it\u2019s the kind of charm that can end a Wyld Hunt for sure, and in short order. Combine that with Octopus and Spider Barrage as well, so if all your enemies declare a ton of defensive charms, yay, they just wasted sixty motes and oh still pick the weakest one and annihilate them. They all try to conserve motes by not spending any, and therefore not waste any? Octopus and Spider Barrage every single one of them with some kind of strength based damage adder. At least I think that\u2019s possible I haven\u2019t triple checked everything yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm genuinely not sure how that's supposed to work. If you have to plan for declare charms for the assuption that you might get the entire flurry coming your way this will end your typical Solar circle too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:29:05-08:00","id":1291083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1291076#post1291076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm genuinely not sure how that's supposed to work. If you have to plan for declare charms for the assuption that you might get the entire flurry coming your way this will end your typical Solar circle too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree, it\u2019s really only letting one lunar count as two or three Lunars for a moment. And the strategy falls apart if the lunar gets rushed or if the characters move to short range from eachother. Also, it\u2019s going to be hard to burn 10m,2wp plus a couple motes of excellencey each round and after the first almost anyone will just spread out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T05:11:18-08:00","id":1291096,"title":"","content":"I've thought about it some more and see your point.<br /> <br /> If the Lunar goes all out with this combo and is taken seriously then everyone will end up in a bad way mote-wise (with some of the targets likely wounded or dead), the Lunar's objectives would probably shift to trying to escape so they could recover and attempt this again another day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T05:18:28-08:00","id":1291098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1291096#post1291096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've thought about it some more and see your point.<br /> <br /> If the Lunar goes all out with this combo and is taken seriously then everyone will end up in a bad way mote-wise (with some of the targets likely wounded or dead), the Lunar's objectives would probably shift to trying to escape so they could recover and attempt this again another day.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a definite theme of &quot;flee to fight another day&quot; in their Dexterity Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> I love the &quot;aim at a general direction&quot; Charm, and could definitely see it return for Alchemical Exalted. That moment when a fighter jet or mecha has the enemies in its sights and a host of reticules appears, with a confirmation of &quot;Target Locked!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T06:04:14-08:00","id":1291105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1291098#post1291098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the &quot;aim at a general direction&quot; Charm, and could definitely see it return for Alchemical Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I got to make requests for the Lunar charmset I did ask for Perception based support for ranged characters. So I'm pretty happy with the result so-far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T06:07:40-08:00","id":1291107,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's nice to have some combat stuff that's not actually in the physical attributes (just like it's nice to have non-combat stuff in the physical attributes, like feats of strength or stealth).<br /> <br /> And an Eagle-Eyed archer should definitely have lots of Perception charms.<br /> <br /> I even wonder, since there are charms to use Charisma for Resolve, Strength for attacks, Stamina for parries, and I think someone mentioned another attribute for Join Battle, will Perception have a charm where you can roll it for making ranged attacks instead of Dexterity? That'd be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T06:11:22-08:00","id":1291108,"title":"","content":"This seems like quite a nice, not overly-mechanical thread, so I'm a bit hesitant to post this, but it's probably relevant.<br /> <br /> Me and my friends were discussing Lunar accuracy charms vs Solar accuracy charms (Excellent Strike, Rising Sun Flash), and these were my calculations:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If they both do 1-point stunts (and the Lunar has another attribute at 5, which may be difficult at character gen if they have Dex 5, but is certainly possible:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Solar has 22 dice, +1 success, re-rolling all 1s.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If he gets his flush, it becomes 25 dice, +2 successes, re-rolling 1s.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It costs 12 motes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Lunar has 24 dice, +1 success, re-roll 10s (in the good way).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This costs 11 motes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So basically I'd say the Solar is better if he gets the flush, and the Lunar is better if the Solar didn't.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But the Lunar could instead spend 14 motes to re-roll 3 failures (and on 24 dice, you would get that) with Striking Mospid (since, hey, the Solar used Excellent Strike).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So then the Lunar has essentially 27 dice, +1 success, re-roll 10s (in the good way).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This costs 14 motes.</span></span><br /> <br /> Overall, they look pretty similar to me. The Lunar's charms are slightly less complicated though.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T08:44:49-08:00","id":1291146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1291083#post1291083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Disagree, it\u2019s really only letting one lunar count as two or three Lunars for a moment. And the strategy falls apart if the lunar gets rushed or if the characters move to short range from eachother. Also, it\u2019s going to be hard to burn 10m,2wp plus a couple motes of excellencey each round and after the first almost anyone will just spread out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh interesting, I wasn't even thinking of using it with a ranged weapon. I was more thinking if you're in the thick of a melee you can aim against everyone who's swarming you, and their only option to disperse is to try and disengage. I don't think it's broken, because the Lunar still has to use a turn aiming while in a melee scrum, but it can wipe out a lot of motes.<br /> <br /> Where it gets super powerful is if you have a sister sitting there embattling the enemies while you aim with a bow, but teamwork is a good thing and I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:01:53-08:00","id":1291148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1291108#post1291108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like quite a nice, not overly-mechanical thread, so I'm a bit hesitant to post this, but it's probably relevant.<br /> <br /> Me and my friends were discussing Lunar accuracy charms vs Solar accuracy charms (Excellent Strike, Rising Sun Flash), and these were my calculations:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If they both do 1-point stunts (and the Lunar has another attribute at 5, which may be difficult at character gen if they have Dex 5, but is certainly possible:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Solar has 22 dice, +1 success, re-rolling all 1s.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If he gets his flush, it becomes 25 dice, +2 successes, re-rolling 1s.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It costs 12 motes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Lunar has 24 dice, +1 success, re-roll 10s (in the good way).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This costs 11 motes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So basically I'd say the Solar is better if he gets the flush, and the Lunar is better if the Solar didn't.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But the Lunar could instead spend 14 motes to re-roll 3 failures (and on 24 dice, you would get that) with Striking Mospid (since, hey, the Solar used Excellent Strike).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So then the Lunar has essentially 27 dice, +1 success, re-roll 10s (in the good way).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This costs 14 motes.</span></span><br /> <br /> Overall, they look pretty similar to me. The Lunar's charms are slightly less complicated though.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having a little trouble with your math here, can you specify which charms besides the excellency each character is using. I get the solar is spending 8m on her excellency for +8 dice (I assume these are withering attacks with mundane medium weapons attacks) gains one success from excellent strike and adds +2 more dice from the stunt and from accuracy and re-rolls 1s. Not sure if a Full excellency means maxing our your pool ornactually spending motes on the excellency, but if the second is true then you gain no successes from excellent strike if you want to potentially use rising sun slash (because successes count against the dice cap). So depending on the ruling (I\u2019m inclined to say you just have to max our your pool) that\u2019s 12 dice baseline, two from stunt , 8 dice from excellency and one success from excellent strike + re-roll 1s. For 22 dice total, one success and re-roll 1s (10% chance per dice of a re-roll). This costs 11m. If the flush is rolled it costs 12m and has 24 dice, two successes.<br /> <br /> Lunar wise, assuming he spends 10m maxing out a 10 dice on an excellency, Plus 2 dice from weapon and two dice from anstunt and re-rolling up to three 1s, which on a normal distribution dice roll (hypothetical) should cover all of the 1s she rolls. But she does not roll them until they fail to appear, so they are just as likely to turn up as 1s the second time. If she uses striking mospid she rolls another two dice (she\u2019s all but guaranteed to roll two failures). She also ignores a point of Parry, which I assume can\u2019t be negated by dipping swallow because it\u2019s not technically a penalty. We\u2019ll say for now that\u2019s the equivalent of a non-charm success. So the lunar is paying 13m to gain 10 dice plus one success but that success is context driven and will in certain circumstances provide no benefit. So she has 24 dice ignores a point of Parry but may re-roll fewer 1s and is not guaranteed to negate all 1s which is a liability against the solar\u2019s more economical Hail Shattering Practice. This also costs her 13m same as the solar and is arguably marginally better or about the same as the solar\u2019s 22 +1 success if you factor in rising sun slash. It is definitely worse, however if dipping swallow can reset defense to its normal value. So that requires clarrification.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know where the 10s re-rolling is coming from. But it\u2019s possible I missed something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290829-lunar-vs-solar-combat-dexterity-charms-preview-discussion?p=1291146#post1291146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh interesting, I wasn't even thinking of using it with a ranged weapon. I was more thinking if you're in the thick of a melee you can aim against everyone who's swarming you, and their only option to disperse is to try and disengage. I don't think it's broken, because the Lunar still has to use a turn aiming while in a melee scrum, but it can wipe out a lot of motes.<br /> <br /> Where it gets super powerful is if you have a sister sitting there embattling the enemies while you aim with a bow, but teamwork is a good thing and I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I figure as a ranged charm its actually much more effective because its pre-req can drop its willpower cost at a far enough range so you can expidite the aiming process when your allies crash characters, also busting out a bunch of low accuracy decisive attacks-- even as a flurry, isn't likely to force character's to spend much on defense against the initial attack. And if you enhance the initial attack enough to make it a threat you're blowing through probably like 15-18m 2wp just to force the expenditure of maybe 10m net more than you would if you had just attacked on two consecutive turns with a 10m excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 02-23-2019, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T14:55:50-08:00","id":1291261,"title":"","content":"Honestly my only issue was having a multiple action withering charm that could focus target on a single individual via Thousand Claw Affliction.<br /> <br /> Weren't we trying to avoid such crap? Multiple decisive attacks don't matter as much as you often don't need soak or threshold successes. With withering you do need to care about such things and it slows down the game. Not only that but it allows you to focus fire on opponents, something Solar thrown doesn't have the luxury of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}